{
  "Comment": "CloudLab c240g5, Wikipedia: task migration (E6) at 90 s, every partition of n4 to n5, a node that joins, under lazy with FetchExtra 0. n4 is not drained: it stays the holder of its raw vectors, which n5 fetches on demand only (Koala's fetch-on-demand): the migration returns after the flip, and n4 holds them to the end. The load stays at the 4 -> 8 runs' first rate, 560 q/s (0.6 x C4 938, 2026-11-20), for 1200 s. StageTimeout 1h: the background part waits for n5's writer, about 7-8.6K 4 KB vectors a second.",
